Subject: [PATCH 04691/11362] [outer-loop] Generation program: RETIRE the
 strong-inducer G0 (already done as exp4883 + logically superseded)

Not-done-before check (operator-directed) on the proposed G0 strong-vs-weak inducer probe:
- ALREADY DONE: experiment_4883_inducer_ceiling_ab (.450 A1b) ran exactly that A/B -- local
  Qwen3.5-9B-MTP vs reference Family-B executable-world-model inducer (arXiv:2605.05138, the same
  SOTA anchor G0 cited), 9 held-out games -> inducer_ceiling_attribution: METHOD_IS_CEILING,
  'neither lane lifts'. (Caveat: that artifact is flagged_adversarial / DURATION_TOO_SHORT and its
  reference lane was a capability_ceiling_only placeholder, so the CLEAN strong-inducer run is
  technically un-run.)
- LOGICALLY SUPERSEDED: exp4914 WALL_IS_HIDDEN_STATE (minimal_abstraction_is_observable_subset=False)
  -- if the winning-prefix-order variable is unobservable from frames, NO inducer however strong can
  plan a prefix whose ordering depends on a variable absent from its inputs. Inducer strength is
  downstream of the observability problem; a clean re-run's outcome is foregone. Expected value ~0.

CORRECTION: Branch A (inducer strength) is refuted. The program proceeds DIRECTLY to Branch B (the
perception->symbolic-state interface): make the hidden interaction-order state OBSERVABLE so the
proposal distribution can assemble the winning prefix; fall back to model-free exploration with an
interaction-history cell key if the state is unrecoverable. The doc now flags that G0' (the Branch-B
probe) must get its OWN not-done-before check before building (it overlaps the nulled NGU/RND exp4688
+ the unbuilt AMAGO/Algorithm-Distillation mapping exp4697 -- must be NEW vs both).

Lesson banked: run the exclusion/rerun check BEFORE proposing a build, not after.

